JDK@cunyvms1.gc.cuny.edu (KASTIN JONATHAN) writes:
{K} Somebody suggested a while ago that in Wizard mode, one should be able to
{K} request special levels (ones with shops, zoos, etc.). I believe it was also
{K} suggested that one should be able to create fountains, thrones, etc.

Well you can do most of that already in wizard mode.

Founains are about the only thing you are unable to create at will.

The game looks for an environment variable (I do believe called SHOPTYPE)
and if it is set to a char like
	Z == zoo
	M == morgue
	B == beehive
	\ == throne
	S == barracks
	_ == temple
	} == swamp
	) == weapon shop
	[ == armor shop
	...  you get the idea.

the game *will* create a room of the type specified on every level
whether it belongs there or not.

